# Case Content Schema Rules

- Source of truth is `content/cases/<id>.json`; `js/data.js` is generated from it by `scripts/build-pages.py`.
- Preserve a stable minimum schema for each case: `order`, `id`, `title`, `address`, `format`, `style`, `segment`, `complex`, `cover`, `summary`, `gallery`, `cta`.
- Keep `id` unique, URL-safe (lowercase kebab-case) and equal to the JSON filename and the `assets/<id>/` folder.
- Keep booleans (`hasVideo`, `hasProjectRender`) aligned with actual payload presence.
- Ensure `cover` equals an existing master image in `assets/<id>/` (never a `-640`/`-1024`/`.webp` variant).
- Ensure each `gallery` item has `src` (master file) and meaningful `alt`.
- Keep link fields valid and absolute (`https://...`) for messenger and social links.
- `metrikaId` and site-wide contacts live in `content/site.json`.

## Consistency Guardrails

- Do not mix unrelated object styles inside one file unless required by runtime.
- Avoid trailing placeholder copy before release.
- Prefer additive updates over broad rewrites of existing case objects.
- After edits run `python scripts/build-pages.py` and `python scripts/validate-cases.py`.
